        "right": 913,
        "scrollable": false,
        "text": "Here\u0027s the full overview, split into the tech stack and the Colab work.\n\n## Project overview\n\nVisionHealth AI is a prototype wellness screening app. A standard Android phone streams its front camera to a Python server on the same Wi-Fi network. The server does the analysis and sends results back to the phone. It is a screening aid, not a medical device, and nothing is diagnosed.\n\n## Tech stack\n\n*Phone app (client)*\n- *Kotlin* and *Android Studio*: the app language and development environment\n- *CameraX*: camera capture, with auto-exposure and white balance locked during measurement\n- *OkHttp*: WebSocket connection to the server, plus HTTP calls for the risk report\n- *Jetpack components*: ViewModel, LiveData, and lifecycle scope for the screens\n- ... Read more",
        "top": 253
